claim.claim-text:
(a) repeatedly determining pressure within the chamber while withdrawing a first volume of air from the chamber;
(b) calculating second-derivative values of pressure with respect to time;
(c) calculating a summation of positive differences between consecutive second derivative values;
(d) comparing the summation to a threshold value;
(e) determining that the summation is greater than the threshold value; and
(f) in response to determining that the summation is greater than the threshold value, increasing the pressure in the chamber.

(a) repeatedly determining pressure within the chamber while withdrawing a third volume of air from the chamber;
(b) calculating second-derivative values of pressure with respect to time corresponding to withdrawing the third volume of air from the chamber;
(c) calculating a second summation of positive differences between consecutive second derivative values;
(d) comparing the second summation to a second threshold value;
(e) determining that the second summation is less than the second threshold value; and
(f) in response to determining that the second summation is less than the second threshold value, introducing a sterilant into the chamber.

(a) repeatedly determining pressure within the chamber while withdrawing a volume of air from the chamber;
(b) calculating second-derivative values of pressure with respect to time;
(c) calculating a summation of positive differences between consecutive second derivative values;
(d) comparing the summation to a threshold value;
(e) determining that the summation is less than the second threshold value; and
(f) in response to determining that the summation is less than the threshold value, introducing a sterilant into the chamber.
